{"id":"a1-u06","level":"a1","order":6,"title":{"en":"Science","fr":"La science","es":"La ciencia","ar":"العلوم"},"tip":{"en":"Scientific writing prefers the passive voice: 'The samples were analysed' rather than 'We analysed the samples'. It puts the focus on the result, not the person.","fr":"L'écrit scientifique préfère la voix passive : « Les échantillons ont été analysés » plutôt que « Nous avons analysé les échantillons ». Elle met l'accent sur le résultat, pas sur la personne.","es":"La escritura científica prefiere la voz pasiva: «Las muestras fueron analizadas» en lugar de «Analizamos las muestras». Pone el foco en el resultado, no en la persona.","ar":"تفضّل الكتابة العلمية المبني للمجهول: «حُلّلت العينات» بدل «حللنا العينات». فهي تركّز على النتيجة لا على الشخص."},"words":49,"lessons":[{"id":"a1-u06-l1","type":"learn","order":1,"title":{"en":"research, scientist, laboratory","fr":"recherche, scientifique, laboratoire","es":"investigación, científico, laboratorio","ar":"بحث، عالِم، مختبر"},"count":11},{"id":"a1-u06-l2","type":"learn","order":2,"title":{"en":"theory, data, sample","fr":"théorie, données, échantillon","es":"teoría, datos, muestra","ar":"نظرية، بيانات، عينة"},"count":10},{"id":"a1-u06-l3","type":"learn","order":3,"title":{"en":"discovery, invention, breakthrough","fr":"découverte, invention, percée","es":"descubrimiento, invento, avance decisiva","ar":"اكتشاف، اختراع، إنجاز علمي"},"count":11},{"id":"a1-u06-l4","type":"learn","order":4,"title":{"en":"effect, correlation, variable","fr":"effet, corrélation, variable","es":"efecto, correlación, variable","ar":"أثر، ارتباط، متغير"},"count":10},{"id":"a1-u06-l5","type":"learn","order":5,"title":{"en":"energy, gravity, atom","fr":"énergie, gravité, atome","es":"energía, gravedad, átomo","ar":"طاقة، جاذبية، ذرة"},"count":11},{"id":"a1-u06-l6","type":"learn","order":6,"title":{"en":"gene, evolution, species","fr":"gène, évolution, espèce","es":"gen, evolución, especie","ar":"جين، تطور، نوع حي"},"count"